  "verses": {
    "verse": [
      [
        "Tell me the tales that to me were so dear,",
        "long, long ago, long, long ago;",
        "sing me the songs I delighted to hear,",
        "long, long ago, long ago.",
        "Now you are come, all my grief is removed,",
        "let me forget that so long you have roved,",
        "let me believe that you love as you loved,",
        "long, long ago, long ago."
      ],
      [
        "Do you remember the path where we met,",
        "long, long ago, long, long ago?",
        "Ah, yes, you told me you ne'er would forget,",
        "long, long ago, long ago.",
        "Then, to all others, my smile you preferred,",
        "love, when you spoke, gave a charm to each word,",
        "still my heart treasures the praises I heard",
        "long, long ago, long ago."
      ],
      [
        "Though by your kindness my fond hopes were raised,",
        "long, long ago, long, long ago,",
        "you by more eloquent lips have been praised,",
        "long, long ago, long ago.",
        "But by long absence your truth has been tried,",
        "still to your accents I listen with pride,",
        "blest as I was when I sat by your side",
        "long, long ago, long ago."
      ]
    ]
  },
  "arrangerNotes": "Visually verified from scan: the voice part was read note by note from the saved page scan (zoomed crops with staff-line pitch guides and notehead detection, each bar checked by eye), and every bar's beat total was confirmed by script; the transcription is saved in scores/scan/ next to the scan PDF. Verse 1, voice part (bars 1–16 after the piano introduction). Slurred notes (bars 9–12) carry one syllable over two notes. No simplification needed. Range low 5 to 6. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–3: Thomas Haynes Bayly, read from the same Cramer, Addison & Beale first edition (c. 1839) the melody was transcribed from, where verses 2 and 3 are engraved under the same notes (printed pages 3–5; scan on Wikimedia Commons, saved in scores/scan/).",
  "verified": true
}
